# Copy to mcps.env and fill in. Gitignored via the repo's existing `*.env`
# pattern — same reasoning as neuralops/infra.env and neuralops/app.env.
#
# Only fill in the integrations you actually want. A service left blank will
# still start, but every tool call against it fails auth — which surfaces in
# chat as the persona saying it couldn't reach the tool, not as a container
# crash. If an integration isn't in use, comment out its whole service block
# in docker-compose.mcps.yaml instead of leaving it running with no token.

# =========================================================
# Monday.com
# =========================================================
# Personal API token. In monday.com: click your avatar (bottom left) →
# Administration → Connections → API → "My access tokens". On some plans it
# sits under Profile → Developers → My Access Tokens instead.
#
# The token inherits YOUR permissions — it can see and modify every board
# your account can. There is no read-only scope on a personal token, so for
# anything beyond a demo, use a dedicated service account with access limited
# to the boards you want exposed.
MONDAY_TOKEN=

# =========================================================
# Jira (Atlassian Cloud)
# =========================================================
# JIRA_URL       your site root, e.g. https://yourcompany.atlassian.net
#                (no trailing slash, no /jira suffix)
# JIRA_USERNAME  the Atlassian account email — not the display name
# JIRA_API_TOKEN create at:
#                https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens
#
# On a company-managed site, creating API tokens can be restricted by an org
# admin — worth checking before you need it. Same permission caveat as
# Monday: the token acts as that user across every project they can reach.
JIRA_URL=
JIRA_USERNAME=
JIRA_API_TOKEN=

# =========================================================
# Web search (SerpAPI)
# =========================================================
# https://serpapi.com/manage-api-key — free tier is 100 searches/month, which
# is fine for demos but will run out under real use. Each persona turn that
# searches consumes at least one credit, sometimes several if the model
# retries.
SERPAPI_KEY=
